protests at more than a dozen clark  county schools  it's part of a call by many parents to  bring all not some students back to the  classroom  soon pre-k through third grade children  are expected back on campus march first  bianca holman reports from one of  several rallies across the valley  cheers and waves in front of foothill  high school parents and students here  want  all students to have the option to  return to school and activities  these rallies come after a recent ccsd  survey in which parents had only  two options to choose from either their  kids will learn virtually  or learn through the hybrid model  parents fear that ccsd will use the  information as an outline for not only  the spring semester  but also the start of school in august  elijah and kylie are high school seniors  who don't want to be forgotten  they say learning online is frustrating  at times making it hard to reach their  full potential  so if they let us get back into school  it'll be a lot easier to learn  and plus if we get sports back  everyone's grades will go up  because that's a lot of people that's  the reason they do good in school is  because of sports  we should be setting the pace not  following the pack  we're nevada step forward we're the  silver state  battle born let's get going currently  ccsd has no plans of allowing kids back  into the classroom full time  parents here want this topic to be  discussed at the next ccsd board meeting  reporting from college and horizon drive  bianca holman  8 news now
 

